{
  "name": "Radar Inbox",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Radar inbox\n\nDrains the aggregator inbox, splits each alert email into individual roles, dedupes on URL hash, scores new roles against the CV and preferences, and writes them to SQLite. All logic lives in scripts/process_email.py, this workflow is only the trigger, the hand-off and the label steps.\n\nThe trigger keys on labels alone, not read state, so opening an email on the phone cannot hide it from the pipeline. An email that fails extraction stays unlabelled and is retried. After three failed attempts the script reports give_up and the workflow shelves the email under radar-failed, so a poison message costs at most three attempts. The digest stats line counts shelved emails since the last digest.\n\nArming steps.\n1. Create the Gmail labels radar-processed and radar-failed in the aggregator account once.\n2. Attach your Gmail OAuth credential to the trigger node and all three Gmail nodes.\n3. Put the real label ids into Label Processed and Label Failed. n8n shows them in the label picker.\n4. Set repo_path and python_bin in the Config node to match the n8n host, and make sure .env with ANTHROPIC_API_KEY and the CV in config/profile/ sit in the repo on that host.\n5. Run once manually, then check the scores in SQLite before activating.\n\nNothing here sends email. Labelling and marking read are the only writes to the mailbox.",
        "width": 460,
        "height": 480
      },
      "id": "9c1f7a10-4a01-4f6e-8b0e-000000000101",
      "name": "How this works",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -560,
        -120
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "pollTimes": {
          "item": [
            {
              "mode": "everyHour"
            }
          ]
        },
        "simple": false,
        "filters": {
          "q": "-label:radar-processed -label:radar-failed"
        },
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "9c1f7a10-4a01-4f6e-8b0e-000000000102",
      "name": "Gmail Trigger",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.gmailTrigger",
      "typeVersion": 1.2,
      "position": [
        -40,
        40
      ],
      "credentials": {
        "gmailOAuth2": {
          "id": "REPLACE_AFTER_IMPORT",
          "name": "Gmail - Radar Aggregator"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "assignments": {
          "assignments": [
            {
              "id": "cfg-repo-path",
              "name": "repo_path",
              "value": "/data/medtech-radar",
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "id": "cfg-python-bin",
              "name": "python_bin",
              "value": "python3",
              "type": "string"
            }
          ]
        },
        "includeOtherFields": true,
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "9c1f7a10-4a01-4f6e-8b0e-000000000103",
      "name": "Config",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.set",
      "typeVersion": 3.4,
      "position": [
        180,
        40
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "mode": "runOnceForEachItem",
        "jsCode": "// Pack the email fields into the JSON contract process_email.py expects,\n// then base64 encode it so no shell quoting can break the command line.\n// The encoded payload travels as one command line argument, which the Linux\n// host caps at 128 KiB, so body_html is dropped whenever body_text exists\n// and both fields are capped well under the limit. The extractor reads at\n// most 12000 chars of body text anyway.\nconst src = $('Gmail Trigger').item.json;\nconst pick = (...vals) => vals.find(v => typeof v === 'string' && v.length) || '';\nlet fromField = '';\nif (src.from && typeof src.from === 'object') {\n  fromField = src.from.text || (src.from.value && src.from.value[0] && src.from.value[0].address) || '';\n} else {\n  fromField = pick(src.from, src.From);\n}\nconst bodyText = pick(src.text, src.textPlain, src.snippet);\nconst bodyHtml = bodyText ? '' : pick(src.html, src.textHtml);\nconst email = {\n  subject: pick(src.subject, src.Subject),\n  from: fromField,\n  date: pick(src.date, src.Date),\n  body_text: bodyText.slice(0, 16000),\n  body_html: bodyHtml.slice(0, 60000),\n};\nreturn {\n  json: {\n    repo_path: $json.repo_path,\n    python_bin: $json.python_bin,\n    b64: Buffer.from(JSON.stringify(email), 'utf8').toString('base64'),\n    messageId: src.id,\n  },\n};"
      },
      "id": "9c1f7a10-4a01-4f6e-8b0e-000000000104",
      "name": "Pack Email",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        400,
        40
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "command": "={{ $json.python_bin }} {{ $json.repo_path }}/scripts/process_email.py --b64 {{ $json.b64 }}"
      },
      "id": "9c1f7a10-4a01-4f6e-8b0e-000000000105",
      "name": "Process Email",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.executeCommand",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        620,
        40
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "mode": "runOnceForEachItem",
        "jsCode": "// Turn the script stdout into a clean result item for the gates.\nlet out = { ok: false, processed: 0, new: 0, duplicates: 0,\n            extract_failed: false, give_up: false, attempts: 0 };\ntry {\n  const raw = ($json.stdout || '').trim();\n  const parsed = JSON.parse(raw.slice(raw.indexOf('{')));\n  out = { ...out, ok: true, ...parsed };\n} catch (err) {\n  out.error = String(err);\n  out.stderr = $json.stderr || '';\n}\nreturn { json: out };"
      },
      "id": "9c1f7a10-4a01-4f6e-8b0e-000000000106",
      "name": "Parse Result",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        840,
        40
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
